--TEST--
`nvs config dump --origin` lists a secret as a row of its own, redacted, with the file its value came from — `rule:config/a-secret-is-a-file-whose-content-is-the-value` and `rule:config/check-and-dump-audit-the-tree-offline`
--RUN--
config dump --origin
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Not run: `--RUN--` names § 9's audit, which reads the tree out of this
// directory rather than a program off argv. This is the program the tree
// governs, and the value it would read is the one the dump refuses to print.
echo Core\Config::get('db.main.password'), "\n";
--FILE nvs.toml--
# § 7's shape: the value is a file, and the file is what the tree names.
[db.main]
driver = "postgres"
password_file = "secrets/db"
--FILE secrets/db--
s3cr3t
--EXPECTF--
db.main.driver        = "postgres"      %snvs.toml
db.main.password      = <secret>        %ssecrets%edb
db.main.password_file = "secrets/db"    %snvs.toml
